  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Evidence-Based Migration Management in the Western Balkans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2017, mixed migration flows have increased significantly in the Western Balkan (WB) region, emphasizing the critical role that WB partners including Albania, Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH), Montenegro, North Macedonia, Serbia and Kosovo* (WB6) can play in improving migration management along this important route.The overall objective of the project is to strengthen Western Balkan partners&apos; capacities to sustainably address mixed migration flows. Using the IOM Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) tools and methodologies, the project will support the systematic collection and analysis of migration flow data, and provide critical information on migrants&apos; presence, profiles, experience and intentions. Furthermore, the project will build local capacities for data collection, analysis, and informed migration response. Moreover, IOM will support dialogues and capacity-building for the Western Balkans partners to build more effective return, reintegration and readmission systems and foster access to Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration (AVRR) to help migrants make informed choices about returning to their country of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
